<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso II of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 759–<a href="/years/842">842</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Alfonso the Chaste</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso II, called the Chaste, was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 791 to 842. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oviedo">Oviedo</a> his capital, modelled his court and church on the Visigothic kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>, resisted repeated Umayyad raids and kept contact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>. During his reign the supposed tomb of Saint James was discovered at Compostela, and he built the first church there, beginning a great pilgrimage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Alfonso II of Asturias" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pelagius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfonsobig.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
